 r←normaliseEvent event;int;n;d;e

 :If ∧/2≤|≡¨event
     r←⊃,/normaliseEvent¨event
 :Else
     int←(10|⎕DR¨event)∊1 3
     n←1⌈(¯1+≢int)⌊+/∧\int ⍝ Event is all leading numbers (but not the last element)
     e←n↑event ⋄ d←n↓event
     e←⊃⍣(3=≡e)⊢e          ⍝ Disclose vector of vectors or event names
     d←⊃⍣(1=≢d)⊢d          ⍝ Disclose when no left argument
     ⍝ ('Event'(1 2)'CB') registers BOTH events, and the codes arrive enclosed
     ⍝ as a single element. Without splitting them they become one bogus event
     ⍝ whose name is the vector "1 2", which then matches nothing.
     :If 1=≢e
     :AndIf (1<≢⊃e)∧(10|⎕DR⊃e)∊1 3
         e←⊃e
     :EndIf
     r←↓(⍪e),⊂d
 :EndIf
